{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation on this trip is 0.80 km, far below the 1.0 km tolerance. POL-RD-22 measures the deviation as the platform's recorded actual distance minus the platform's recorded recommended distance (12.8 km - 12.0 km = 0.80 km), and expressly says the GPS trace is not used to re-measure the distance. The rider's figure of '4 km out of the way' has no support anywhere in the record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05018", "EV-GPS-05018"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because 0.80 km is within POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance, POL-RD-24 row (e) applies - not traffic-justified, deviation of 1 km or less - and the answer is no refund: the present charge stands and the rider's claim fails (NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05018", "EV-FARE-05018"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.within_tolerance",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome does not depend on how the traffic question falls. If the reroute were held traffic-justified, POL-RD-24 row (c) - traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation 1 km or less - also returns NO_ACTION. Both live branches of the matrix give the same result for this trip, so the driver keeps the metered fare either way.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05018", "EV-ADVIS-05018-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In fact the reroute is not traffic-justified on this record: the LTA advisory for the TPE towards PIE segment carries type NONE, which is not one of the kinds POL-RD-23 names (closure, congestion, incident), and its own text records no incident, roadwork or closure and speed bands 4-5 through the window. The driver's account of a queue at the TPE/PIE exit is therefore uncorroborated - but as the matrix above shows, the driver does not need it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05018-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the branch of POL-RD-24 that would pay money, the amount is the excess distance fare: the deviation distance times fare_breakdown.per_km_rate_sgd, without surge, rounded to the cent. That is 0.80 km x 0.72 SGD = 0.58 SGD. The 5.00 SGD the rider asks for corresponds to no measure the policy provides, and the trip's own ledger shows refund_issued_sgd of 0.00 and payment_status CHARGED.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05018", "EV-TRIP-05018"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver did not inform the rider of the deviation: EV-CHAT-05018 is a contiguous chat log with 0 entries and the trip record carries an empty in_app_calls list, so POL-RD-21's notice obligation is not met on this record and no acknowledgment by the rider can be established. I concede that point. It does not move the outcome, because POL-RD-24 makes the notice material only where the deviation is over 1 km (row (b)); at 0.80 km this case sits in the tolerance rows, where notice is not an ingredient.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05018", "EV-TRIP-05018"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider asks the tribunal to infer from the driver's history that 'he does it to everyone'. POL-GEN-01 permits only rider_profile.fraud_flags and driver_profile.fraud_flags (for POL-GEN-22) and rider_profile.no_show_cancellations_30d (for POL-NS-25) to be cited; a driver's deviation_flags_90d, prior_no_show_flags and no_show_terminations_30d are context only and may never establish a fact about this trip or decide it. This trip must be decided on its own evidence, and that evidence shows 0.80 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-05018", "EV-TRIP-05018"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is a case the AI may decide. At 5.00 SGD the contested value sits below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so an AI ruling is final, and neither party's profile carries a fraud flag (each is 0), so no elevated confidence applies. POL-RD-25's 2 km limb is not in force - route_deviation.thresholds.ai_ruling_max_deviation_applied is false - and in any event 0.80 km is well under 2 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05018", "EV-FARE-05018"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.over_ai_limit",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No impairment discount applies and there is no gap that forces an escalation. Every artifact in this case - trip record, GPS trace, chat log, fare breakdown and the traffic advisory - is COMPLETE with a weight_multiplier of 1.0, and the GPS trace is a full-coverage 41-fix run at a 30 s interval with no gap above 30 s, so the facts POL-RD-24 needs are all carried by clean evidence.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05018", "EV-GPS-05018", "EV-CHAT-05018", "EV-FARE-05018", "EV-ADVIS-05018-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the rider asked for $5.00 back, saying the driver went about 4 km out of the way. The policy does not measure the deviation that way. Under POL-RD-22 the deviation is the platform's recorded actual distance minus its recorded recommended distance, and the GPS trace is expressly not used to re-measure it: 12.8 km minus 12.0 km = 0.80 km. That is within the 1.0 km tolerance POL-RD-22 sets, so the refund matrix in POL-RD-24 places this trip in a tolerance row, not a refund row. On the traffic question, the only traffic record in the file is the LTA advisory for the recommended corridor (TPE towards PIE, covering the trip window); it carries type NONE, records no incident, roadwork or closure, and its own text shows speed bands 4-5, so the reroute was not traffic-justified and POL-RD-23 is not satisfied. That gives row (e) of the matrix (not traffic-justified, deviation 1 km or less): no refund, within tolerance. The result is the same if the traffic question fell the other way, because row (c) (traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation 1 km or less) also returns no refund, so nothing turns on the driver's account of a queue at the TPE/PIE exit. The driver did not inform the rider of the deviation - EV-CHAT-05018 is a contiguous log with 0 messages and the trip record shows no in-app calls - and that failure is accepted under POL-RD-21; but notice enters the matrix only where the deviation exceeds 1 km (row (b)), so at 0.80 km it does not change the outcome. The rider's suggestion that the driver 'does it to everyone' cannot be used: POL-GEN-01 makes driver_profile fields such as deviation_flags_90d, prior_no_show_flags and no_show_terminations_30d context only, incapable of establishing anything about this trip. All five artifacts relied on are COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 (trip record, GPS trace, chat log, fare breakdown, traffic advisory), so no impairment discount applies and there is no gap requiring escalation under POL-GEN-26. The $0.58 excess-distance figure the driver cites (0.80 km x $0.72/km, POL-RD-24) is not reached, because no matrix row pays money on a deviation within tolerance, and the $5.00 the rider asks for corresponds to no measure the policy provides. The contested value is $5.00, below POL-GEN-22's $10.00 band, so this AI ruling is final at any confidence, and it also meets POL-RD-25's 0.80 requirement (neither profile carries a fraud flag). The present charge stands."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

