    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider, your $5.00 claim is not supported; driver, the metered fare stands.\n\nThe deviation is measured only from the platform's recorded distances, as POL-RD-22 requires: actual 12.8 km minus recommended 12.0 km = 0.80 km (EV-TRIP-05018). POL-RD-22 expressly says the GPS trace is not used to re-measure distance, so the trace neither confirms the '4 km out of the way' figure in your complaint nor displaces the record; the 0.80 km stands. At 0.80 km the deviation is within POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance.\n\nThat fixes the refund matrix. POL-RD-24 row (e) - not traffic-justified, deviation 1 km or less - returns NO_ACTION, and were the traffic question to fall the other way, row (c) - traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation 1 km or less - returns NO_ACTION as well. So neither the traffic-justification question nor the notice question changes the result.\n\nOn those two questions, both answered against the driver but with no effect on the outcome: the only traffic record in the file, the LTA advisory for the TPE towards PIE segment valid across the whole trip window (EV-ADVIS-05018-01), carries type NONE and records no incident, roadwork or closure with speed bands 4-5, so POL-RD-23 traffic justification is not made out; and the contiguous chat log holds 0 messages and the trip record holds no in-app calls (EV-CHAT-05018, EV-TRIP-05018), so POL-RD-21 notice was not given. At 0.80 km these two findings sit in the matrix's tolerance rows and move nothing.\n\nThe excess distance fare, had a refund been due, would be the deviation distance times the per-km rate, without surge: 0.80 km x 0.72 SGD = 0.58 SGD (EV-FARE-05018, POL-RD-24). The 5.00 SGD you ask for corresponds to no measure the policy provides. The suggestion that the driver 'does it to everyone' cannot be used: under POL-GEN-01 every profile field other than the two fraud_flags and the no-show field is context only and may not establish a fact about this trip or decide it.\n\nAll artifacts are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so no impairment discount applies and no fact is left unestablished (POL-GEN-02, POL-GEN-26). The contested value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, no fraud flag (0) and no safety flag apply, so the AI decides this finally at the 0.80 confidence POL-RD-25 requires. POL-RD-24's own labels are used: neither branch that could pay returns the whole trip fare.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
